## R-164 — CI finding on PR #189 after the review fixes
CI run 39159170212 (head 66eda13), job test, one Python 3.12 run: FAILED tests/test_r164_backpressure.py::test_r164_web_pool_saturation_does_not_stall_local_net_or_storage — assert load['waiting'] == 3 -> 2 == 3; the other runs: 1493 passed.
cause: pools.run's queue cap read ThreadPoolExecutor._work_queue.qsize(), which also counts calls that IDLE threads have not picked up yet -> in a burst the cap refused calls (PoolBusy) while threads were free; load()['waiting'] was off for the same reason.

